As argued in https://github.com/rstudio/rmarkdown/issues/1343, I believe that pkgdown output should feature the small 10px spacer between the bottom of html widgets and the succeeding content too, similarly to paragraphs or code chunks. Otherwise the widgets "stick" on top of the blocks following them, as it is currently the case (see e.g. the [rendered example](https://giscience.github.io/openrouteservice-r/articles/openrouteservice.html)).

This could be easily fixed by adding the CSS rule to [pkgdown.css](https://github.com/r-lib/pkgdown/blob/master/inst/assets/pkgdown.css):

```css
.html-widget {
  margin-bottom: 10px;
}
